  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Józef Wojciechowski is a Polish property developer who founded J.W. Construction after building businesses in the United States. Trained in economics in Sopot, he returned to Poland and established the company in 1993. Residential construction became its core activity, with housing developments drawing on his earlier experience in the American market.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 95,
      "band": "very_high",
      "reason": "Primary company biography and independent reporting establish career and education."
    },
    "source_ids": [
      "S1",
      "S2"
    ],
    "word_count": 52,
    "html": "<p>Józef Wojciechowski is a Polish property developer who founded J.W. Construction after building businesses in the United States. Trained in economics in Sopot, he returned to Poland and established the company in 1993. Residential construction became its core activity, with housing developments drawing on his earlier experience in the American market.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "When Józef Wojciechowski began developing homes in Florida, he kept his business small: an office in his own house, one licensed building professional and subcontractors. He controlled construction costs closely and offered houses below competing prices. Advertising received a larger commitment, with appearances in local newspapers and on television.\n\nA later purchase in Kraków prompted a different decision. Having bought a former bank building, he considered apartments and then a sale. His daughters persuaded him to retain it as an asset for future generations. He instead began converting the building into a luxury hotel, bringing their longer view into the family business.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 94,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Detailed early-business reporting and a direct family interview support both episodes; the hotel is described as a project, not an already completed opening."
    },
    "source_ids": [
      "S2",
      "S4"
    ],
    "word_count": 102,
    "html": "<p>When Józef Wojciechowski began developing homes in Florida, he kept his business small: an office in his own house, one licensed building professional and subcontractors. He controlled construction costs closely and offered houses below competing prices. Advertising received a larger commitment, with appearances in local newspapers and on television.</p>\r\n<p>A later purchase in Kraków prompted a different decision. Having bought a former bank building, he considered apartments and then a sale. His daughters persuaded him to retain it as an asset for future generations. He instead began converting the building into a luxury hotel, bringing their longer view into the family business.</p>\r\n"
  },
